<p>The interior of this map is white, but it appears to be suffused with a pale yellow. In fact the blue and orange coloring is confined to the border.</p>
<p>This &#8220;bleeding&#8221; effect was discovered by University of Sassari psychologist Baingio Pinna in 1987. It&#8217;s still being investigated.</p>
